  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "BESSELI is ITK's published polynomial and recurrence, on the x87 unit",
  "statement": "BESSELI truncates n to an integer and evaluates the body published in ITK with every operation stored from the x87 unit at precision 64: the I0 and I1 polynomials, and for higher orders Miller backward recurrence from j = 2*(n + int(sqrt(40*n))), rescaling by 1E-10 whenever |q| > 1E10, then normalising by I0(x). The same body in plain binary64 misses by 1 to 4 units in the last place. The published ITK body is itkGaussianOperator.hxx at ITK 311b7060ef39e371f3cd209ec135284ff5fde735 (Apache-2.0).",
  "status": "measured",
